<title>BRAZIL: Brazil BNDES to lend $1 bln for aircraft deal.</title>
<headline>Brazil BNDES to lend $1 bln for aircraft deal.</headline>
<dateline>RIO DE JANEIRO 1997-02-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Brazil's National Development Bank (BNDES) has approved a $1 billion loan to finance the export of 40 Embraer EMB 145 jets to the United States, a BNDES spokeswoman said.</p>
<p>She said the BNDES had agreed to the loan and was only waiting for Brazilian aircraft manufacturer Embraer and American Airlines's subsidiary American Eagle to sign the deal.</p>
<p>She said it was the first time the BNDES was financing such a transaction via a so-called &quot;buyer credit&quot;, in which the loan is granted to the buyer of the goods to be exported.</p>
<p>The EMB 145 jet is a 50-passenger aircraft.</p>
<p>((--Simona de Logu, Rio de Janeiro newsroom, 5521 507 4151))</p>
